<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15691" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτί̆-πους</span></b> , ὁ, ἡ, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πουν</span>, τό, gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποδος</span>: 
			Ep.
		 nom. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτίπος</span></b> :
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρτιος,
				πούς</span>) <i>sound of foot,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ μὲν καλός τε καὶ ἀρτίπος,</span>
			opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χωλός,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.31c
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.130
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Them.
				<u>Or.</u>
				21.255c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>strong</i> or <i>swift of foot,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ δ᾽ Ἄτη σθεναρή τε καὶ ἀρτίπος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.505
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτίποδες καὶ ἀρτίχειρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					795d
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρτι, πούς</span>) <i>coming just in time,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				58
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
